  "claim": "Samuel Krachmalnick was the music director of the operetta that Lamplighters Music Theatre features. George Maran came to the attention of this composer.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Lamplighters Music Theatre. Sentence: Founded in 1952 by Orva Hoskinson and Ann Pool MacNab, the Lamplighters specialize in light opera, particularly the works of Gilbert and Sullivan, as well as such works as \"The Merry Widow\", \"Die Fledermaus\", \"Of Thee I Sing\", \"My Fair Lady\", \"Candide\", and \"A Little Night Music\".\nPage: Candide (operetta). Sentence: Candide is an operetta with music composed by Leonard Bernstein, based on the 1759 novella of the same name by Voltaire.\nPage: Samuel Krachmalnick. Sentence: He first came to prominence as a conductor on Broadway during the 1950s, notably earning a Tony Award nomination for his work as the music director of the original production of Leonard Bernstein's \"Candide\".\nPage: George Maran. Sentence: Maran attended Harvard University where he and his voice came to the attention of people such as Leonard Bernstein and Paul Hindemith.",
